module Incomplete.Gu03 where

{- INFERENCE GIVES UP WHERE CHECKING SUCCEEDS -- 3 of 4: the wall.

   THE SCENARIO.  Gu02's order-line view plus the last two dimensions the
   warehouse has: the tax treatment the line was booked under and the promotion
   it was sold on.  Eight dimensions round a fact table is a small star schema;
   real ones have twenty.

   WHAT A COMPETENT USER EXPECTS.  To reload the module and get on with the
   report.

   WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS.  See the header of this file's own measurement below.
   Compile it and nothing comes back.

   THE INCOMPLETENESS.  Same as Gu01/Gu02, one rung further out.  The step
   ratios measured on this definition -- 1.7x, 2.8x, 6.1x, 13.2x, 29.4x as
   dimensions go 2..7 -- put eight dimensions somewhere near two hours, and the
   ratio is still climbing.  Gu04 is THIS EXACT DEFINITION with a signature.
-}

import Prelude
import Relation
import Syntax.Relation

wideOrderLines orderLine productDim regionDim channelDim calendarDim customerDim currencyDim taxDim promoDim =
  orderLine ** productDim ** regionDim ** channelDim ** calendarDim
            ** customerDim ** currencyDim ** taxDim ** promoDim
